{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/OmniLight3D\/omniAttenuation","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Controls the distance attenuation function for omnilights.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"omniAttenuation"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0"},{"text":" will maintain a constant brightness through most of the range, but smoothly attenuate the light at the edge of the range. Use a value of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2.0"},{"type":"text","text":" for physically accurate lights as it results in the proper inverse square attenutation."}]},{"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Setting attenuation to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2.0"},{"type":"text","text":" or higher may result in distant objects receiving minimal light, even within range. For example, with a range of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4096"},{"text":", an object at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"100"},{"text":" units is attenuated by a factor of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0001"},{"type":"text","text":". With a default brightness of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"text":", the light would not be visible at that distance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"style":"note","name":